        "content": "<p>epitaphial opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/15297\">issue #15297</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>wasi-preview1-component-adapter: fd_readdir duplicates a truncated entry after synthetic dot entries</h1>\n<h2>Summary</h2>\n<p>When a 23-byte buffer truncates the first dirent and cookie 0 is used for the next large read, Direct P1 returns <code>.</code>, <code>..</code>, then the directory files. The adapter returns <code>.</code>, <code>..</code>, <code>.</code> again, then the files. This violates split/resume equivalence with one full read.</p>\n<p>Confirmed with the standalone C program below, without any custom test driver or trace format. Each lane reproduced the same output 5/5 times in fresh directories on Wasmtime 46.0.0 (Release and Debug), 47.0.2, and 50.0.1. Wasmtime 50.0.1 was the latest upstream release at verification time.</p>\n<h2>Minimal reproducer (<code>repro.c</code>)</h2>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"C\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"cp\">#define _POSIX_C_SOURCE 200809L</span>\n<span class=\"cp\">#include</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cpf\">&lt;fcntl.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"cp\">#include</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cpf\">&lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"cp\">#include</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cpf\">&lt;string.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"cp\">#include</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cpf\">&lt;sys/stat.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"cp\">#include</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cpf\">&lt;unistd.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"cp\">#include</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"cpf\">&lt;wasi/api.h&gt;</span>\n\n<span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">main</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">void</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kt\">unsigned</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">char</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">small</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">23</span><span class=\"p\">],</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">large</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">4096</span><span class=\"p\">];</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">__wasi_size_t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">used1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">used2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">mkdir</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"testdir\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mo\">0755</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">char</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"sc\">'a'</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"sc\">'d'</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"o\">++</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"kt\">char</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">path</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">32</span><span class=\"p\">];</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">snprintf</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">path</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">sizeof</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">path</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"testdir/%c.txt\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">close</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">open</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">path</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">O_CREAT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">O_WRONLY</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mo\">0644</span><span class=\"p\">));</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">open</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"testdir\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">O_RDONLY</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">O_DIRECTORY</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">__wasi_errno_t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">error1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">__wasi_fd_readdir</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fd</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">small</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">23</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&amp;</span><span class=\"n\">used1</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">__wasi_errno_t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">error2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">__wasi_fd_readdir</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fd</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">large</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4096</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&amp;</span><span class=\"n\">used2</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">printf</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"first: errno=%u used=%u</span><span class=\"se\">\\n</span><span class=\"s\">\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">error1</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">unsigned</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"n\">used1</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">printf</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"second: errno=%u used=%u entries:\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">error2</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">unsigned</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"n\">used2</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">size_t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">offset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">offset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">sizeof</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">__wasi_dirent_t</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">used2</span><span class=\"p\">;)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">__wasi_dirent_t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">entry</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">memcpy</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">&amp;</span><span class=\"n\">entry</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">large</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">offset</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">sizeof</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">entry</span><span class=\"p\">));</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">offset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">sizeof</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">entry</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">entry</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">d_namlen</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">used2</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">break</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">printf</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\" %.*s(next=%llu)\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">int</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"n\">entry</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">d_namlen</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">large</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">offset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">sizeof</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">entry</span><span class=\"p\">),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">               </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">unsigned</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">long</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">long</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"n\">entry</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">d_next</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">offset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">sizeof</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">entry</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">entry</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">d_namlen</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">printf</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"</span><span class=\"se\">\\n</span><span class=\"s\">\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">close</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fd</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<h2>Exact commands</h2>\n<p>Run in a new empty directory. The first command downloads the official v50.0.1 command adapter; <code>clang</code>, <code>wasm-tools</code>, and <code>wasmtime</code> must be on the stated paths or adjusted to local installations.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Bash\"><pre><span></span><code>curl<span class=\"w\"> </span>-fLO<span class=\"w\"> </span>https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/releases/download/v50.0.1/wasi_snapshot_preview1.command.wasm\n/opt/wasi-sdk/bin/clang<span class=\"w\"> </span>--target<span class=\"o\">=</span>wasm32-wasip1<span class=\"w\"> </span>-std<span class=\"o\">=</span>c17<span class=\"w\"> </span>-O2<span class=\"w\"> </span>-Wall<span class=\"w\"> </span>-Wextra<span class=\"w\"> </span>-Werror<span class=\"w\"> </span>repro_rc_dir_split_resume.c<span class=\"w\"> </span>-o<span class=\"w\"> </span>repro_p1.wasm\nwasm-tools<span class=\"w\"> </span>component<span class=\"w\"> </span>new<span class=\"w\"> </span>repro_p1.wasm<span class=\"w\"> </span>--adapt<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">wasi_snapshot_preview1</span><span class=\"o\">=</span>wasi_snapshot_preview1.command.wasm<span class=\"w\"> </span>-o<span class=\"w\"> </span>repro_adapter.wasm\nwasmtime<span class=\"w\"> </span>run<span class=\"w\"> </span>--dir<span class=\"w\"> </span>.<span class=\"w\"> </span>repro_p1.wasm<span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>wasmtime<span class=\"w\"> </span>run<span class=\"w\"> </span>--dir<span class=\"w\"> </span>.<span class=\"w\"> </span>repro_adapter.wasm\n</code></pre></div>\n<h2>Expected vs. actual output (Wasmtime 50.0.1)</h2>\n<p><strong>Direct P1 (expected):</strong></p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Text only\"><pre><span></span><code>first: errno=0 used=23\nsecond: errno=0 used=167 entries: .(next=1) ..(next=2) c.txt(next=3) b.txt(next=4) d.txt(next=5) a.txt(next=6)\n</code></pre></div>\n<p><strong>Adapter P2 (actual):</strong></p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Text only\"><pre><span></span><code>first: errno=0 used=23\nsecond: errno=0 used=192 entries: .(next=1) ..(next=2) .(next=1) c.txt(next=4) b.txt(next=5) d.txt(next=6) a.txt(next=7)\n</code></pre></div>\n<h2>Root cause</h2>\n<p>On truncation, <code>fd_readdir</code> saves the stream, <code>cookie - 1</code>, and <code>cached_dirent</code> (<a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/blob/v50.0.1/crates/wasi-preview1-component-adapter/src/lib.rs#L1502-L1506\"><code>lib.rs:1502-1506</code></a>). On resume, it sets <code>use_cache: true</code> (<a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/blob/v50.0.1/crates/wasi-preview1-component-adapter/src/lib.rs#L1413-L1419\"><code>lib.rs:1413-1419</code></a>). However, <code>DirectoryEntryIterator::next</code> handles synthetic <code>.</code>/<code>..</code> from <code>current_cookie</code> before checking <code>use_cache</code> (<a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/blob/v50.0.1/crates/wasi-preview1-component-adapter/src/lib.rs#L1536-L1571\"><code>lib.rs:1536-1571</code></a>). The cached truncated entry is consequently emitted after the synthetic entries, duplicating it and shifting later cookies. The ordering remains in v50.0.1.</p>\n<h2>Suggested fix and causal evidence</h2>\n<p>When resuming a cached stream, yield <code>cached_dirent</code> before the synthetic dot-entry branches. The existing v46 <code>cookie_resume_fix.patch</code> used that ordering. Across 30 regression cases, violations went from 8 unpatched to 0 patched and back to 8 reverted; the reverted adapter binary matched the original.<br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
